<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?><rss version="2.0"><channel><title>Bing: "DCGS-A Capability Drop 1" offeror</title><link>http://www.bing.com:80/search?q=%22DCGS-A+Capability+Drop+1%22+offeror</link><description>Search results</description><image><url>http://www.bing.com:80/s/a/rsslogo.gif</url><title>"DCGS-A Capability Drop 1" offeror</title><link>http://www.bing.com:80/search?q=%22DCGS-A+Capability+Drop+1%22+offeror</link></image><copyright>Copyright © 2026 Microsoft. All rights reserved. These XML results may not be used, reproduced or transmitted in any manner or for any purpose other than rendering Bing results within an RSS aggregator for your personal, non-commercial use. Any other use of these results requires express written permission from Microsoft Corporation. By accessing this web page or using these results in any manner whatsoever, you agree to be bound by the foregoing restrictions.</copyright><item><title>Rainbow Shops | Affordable Plus Size &amp; Women’s Fashion</title><link>https://www.rainbowshops.com/</link><description>Shop Rainbow for affordable plus size and women’s clothing in sizes XS to 4X. New arrivals daily. Free shipping on $75 and easy in-store returns.</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 15:37:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Rainbow - Wikipedia</title><link>https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rainbow</link><description>The order of a rainbow is determined by the number of light reflections inside the water droplets that create it: One reflection results in the first-order or primary rainbow; two reflections create the second-order or secondary rainbow.</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 11:05:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>7 Rare Sky Phenomena and Types of Rainbows You Can See</title><link>https://www.farmersalmanac.com/types-of-rainbows</link><description>This guide explores seven rare sky phenomena and rainbow types, including double rainbows, moonbows, fogbows, and supernumerary rainbows.</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 00:06:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>The 7 Colors of the Rainbow and Their Meanings Explained in Detail</title><link>https://www.color-meanings.com/colors-of-the-rainbow-and-their-meanings/</link><description>Because of the rainbow’s importance across multiple religions and cultural beliefs, the rainbow is packed with symbolism. Let’s take a look at each of the colors and what they mean.</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 11:19:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>What are the 7 colors of rainbow in order called? - Color With Leo</title><link>https://www.colorwithleo.com/what-are-the-7-colors-of-rainbow-in-order-called/</link><description>So when you see a rainbow, the red band will always be at the top and the violet band at the bottom. This sequence of 7 colors has become well-established in scientific sources and popular culture.</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 15:08:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Rainbow Shops store locations | Clothing Store</title><link>https://stores.rainbowshops.com/</link><description>Directory of Rainbow stores. Find a local Rainbow store near you for clothing, shoes and accessories.</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 14:54:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Rainbow (rock band) - Wikipedia</title><link>https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rainbow_(rock_band)</link><description>Rainbow (also known as Ritchie Blackmore's Rainbow or Blackmore's Rainbow) were a British hard rock band formed in Hertford in 1975 by guitarist Ritchie Blackmore.</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 13:50:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>What Is a Rainbow? - timeanddate.com</title><link>https://www.timeanddate.com/astronomy/rainbow.html</link><description>All about rainbows. What causes a rainbow, why is it curved? What are the rainbow colors, how does a double rainbow work, and what's at rainbow's end?</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 15:30:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>What Causes a Rainbow? | Light, Physics, Reflection, Refraction ...</title><link>https://www.britannica.com/science/What-Causes-a-Rainbow</link><description>A rainbow is caused by the refraction, dispersion, and reflection of sunlight as it passes through raindrops. As light passes through raindrops, it bends at different rates causing it to spread out into the colors of the visible spectrum.</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 08:13:00 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>What are the 12 colors of the rainbow? - Color With Leo</title><link>https://www.colorwithleo.com/what-are-the-12-colors-of-the-rainbow/</link><description>While many of us learn there are 7 colors of the rainbow in school, the full spectrum of colors in a rainbow is made up of 12 distinct bands. Rainbows are optical light phenomena that occur when sunlight interacts with water droplets in the atmosphere.</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 15:30:00 GMT</pubDate></item></channel></rss>